        content: 'The staff on his back was new in a way the road was not. It had come with the robes sometime in the last unmeasured while, along with the knowledge of what it was—light ashwood, a hairline seam of silver down its length—and the memory of Earth had no place to file either one. The grass gave way to packed dirt, the verge narrowed, and the road to Alderwatch took him.\n' +
